<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
  Big and Small's humanlike-ThingDef generator (HumanlikeAnimalGenerator.GenerateAndRegisterHumanlikeAnimal)
  filters every comp on the original animal/mechanoid ThingDef against the merged
  compWhitelist/tabWhitelist/modExtensionWhitelist of every loaded HumanlikeAnimalSettings
  def - anything not listed is silently dropped when it builds the sapient version's
  ThingDef. It ships its own DefaultHumanlikeAnimalSettings (see Big and Small's own
  Defs/Presets/PawnExtensionPresets/HumanlikeAnimalGenerator.xml) covering vanilla/VEF
  comps, but doesn't know about mech-queen-style "carrier" comps, so a sapient Work
  Queen ([AV] Framework) or War Queen (vanilla Biotech) loses its steel reserve and
  urchin-release gizmo entirely - the comps backing them just never make it onto the
  generated ThingDef in the first place. All HumanlikeAnimalSettings defs get merged
  together (see HumanlikeAnimalSettings.AllHASettings), so this only needs to add the
  missing entries, not touch Big and Small's own def.

  Vanilla's War Queen (Mech_Warqueen, Races_Mechanoids_SuperHeavy.xml) combines both
  the steel reserve and the urchin spawning into one CompProperties_MechCarrier.
  [AV] Framework's Work Queen splits the same idea across two comps instead:
  CompProperties_MechReloadableResourceHolder (the reserve) and
  CompProperties_MechCarrierChoice (the release gizmo, letting the player pick which
  urchin type to spawn rather than always the same one).

  Whitelisting the comps only gets them back onto the pawn - it doesn't make their
  gizmos visible again on its own. Both RimWorld.CompMechCarrier and
  AV_Framework.CompMechCarrierChoice/CompMechReloadableResourceHolder additionally gate
  their CompGetGizmosExtra on pawn.IsColonyMech, which Big and Small deliberately clears
  for every sapient mechanoid - see Pawn_IsColonyMech_Patch.cs for that half of the fix.
  -->
  <BigAndSmall.HumanlikeAnimalSettings>
    <defName>SapientMechanoidFix_MechQueenWhitelist</defName>
    <compWhitelist>
      <!-- Vanilla Biotech - War Queen -->
      <li>RimWorld.CompProperties_MechCarrier</li>

      <!-- [AV] Framework - Work Queen -->
      <li>AV_Framework.CompProperties_MechReloadableResourceHolder</li>
      <li>AV_Framework.CompProperties_MechCarrierChoice</li>

      <!-- Vanilla Biotech - auto-repair toggle (all mechanoids). Unlike the two
           above, this one is just a bool field with a gizmo - no lifecycle-hook fix
           needed for the comp itself. See WorkGiver_RepairMech_HasJobOnThing_Patch.cs
           and JobDriver_RepairMech_MakeNewToils_Patch.cs for what it actually takes
           to make auto-repair functional for a sapient mechanoid, since vanilla's own
           repair WorkGiver/JobDriver both assume every mechanoid has a power (energy)
           need, which sapient mechanoids deliberately don't. -->
      <li>RimWorld.CompProperties_MechRepairable</li>

      <!-- Vanilla Biotech - War Queen's mounted turret gun (Gun_ChargeBlasterTurret).
           Without this the sapient clone had no ranged attack at all - just its innate
           melee "head" tool. CompTurretGun.PostPostMake() is what actually constructs
           the gun Thing, and RaceMorpher_AddMissingComps_Patch.cs already calls
           PostPostMake/PostSpawnSetup on every newly-added comp, so this "just works"
           without any comp-specific patch. Its only two mechanoid-specific gates
           (fire-at-will check, toggle-turret gizmo visibility) both key off
           Pawn.IsColonyMechPlayerControlled, already fixed by
           Pawn_IsColonyMechPlayerControlled_Patch.cs. -->
      <li>RimWorld.CompProperties_TurretGun</li>

      <!-- Reactive armor (steel-scaled damage reduction) - see
           CompSapientMechReactiveArmor.cs and Patches/ReactiveArmor.xml, which is what
           actually adds this comp to Mech_Warqueen/AV_Mech_Workerqueen in the first
           place, since it isn't a comp either ThingDef ships with natively. -->
      <li>SapientMechanoidFix.CompProperties_SapientMechReactiveArmor</li>

      <!-- Reactive armor (charge-limited hit-triggered immunity) - see
           CompSapientMechHitArmor.cs. Independent of the comp above; both run
           together. -->
      <li>SapientMechanoidFix.CompProperties_SapientMechHitArmor</li>

      <!-- Glitterworld Destroyer 5 - War Queen's "kill all urchins" button. Its
           gizmo only checks Owner.Faction == Faction.OfPlayer, no mechanoid-specific
           gate at all, so this needs nothing beyond the whitelist entry itself. Only
           ever present if GD5 is installed and has patched Mech_Warqueen - harmless
           whitelist entry otherwise, since it just never matches anything. -->
      <li>GD3.CompProperties_AllDead</li>

      <!-- Glitterworld Destroyer 5 - War Queen's auto-release-urchins toggle
           (periodically calls CompMechCarrier.TrySpawnPawns() on its own). Same
           direct MechanitorUtility.GetOverseer(pawn) == null gizmo-visibility gate as
           AV Framework's two comps - see OverseerGizmoSuppressionPatches.cs, which
           reuses the exact same suppression-window fix for this comp's
           CompGetGizmosExtra too. -->
      <li>GD3.CompProperties_AttackMode</li>
    </compWhitelist>
    <tabWhitelist>
      <li>AV_Framework.ITab_MechQueen</li>
    </tabWhitelist>
  </BigAndSmall.HumanlikeAnimalSettings>

</Defs>
